---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" current="about" description={`About ${site.author}.`}>
  <div class="about-grid">
    <section class="hero" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
      <img class="avatar" src="/avatar.jpg" width="176" height="176" alt={site.author} />
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">About</p>
        <h1>{site.author}</h1>
        <p class="lede">{site.oneLiner}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        I work at the intersection of systems security, AI, and trust. For more than a decade I have
        built and led security programs across cloud, automotive, and digital finance — from kernel
        and confidential-computing research to product-scale software security.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have led security engineering and research at OKX, headed product and software security at
        NIO, led security research at Baidu USA, worked on Knox at Samsung Research America, and
        completed a postdoc at Carnegie Mellon CyLab with Virgil Gligor and Adrian Perrig. I also
        serve as an adjunct professor at the University of Delaware and hold a Ph.D. in
        virtualization-based system security from Singapore Management University.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work covers threat detection, confidential computing, microarchitecture security,
        software supply-chain defenses, and AI security. I have published more than fifty papers and
        hold dozens of granted patents. Black Hat and DEF CON talks are part of that same thread:
        making attacks concrete so defenses can catch up.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is a public notebook for ideas at the boundary of security, trust, innovation, and
        AI — including the occasional hypothesis that does not yet have a category.
      </p>
    </article>

    <p class="links">
      <a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>
      <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a>
      <a href={site.scholar}>Google Scholar</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
